{"type":"message","id":"768d1696","parentId":"a509bf81","timestamp":"2026-05-20T02:32:07.793Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - `/api/send` returns a different response (ECHO Agent Platform v0.2) but still 200. But actually, the second curl returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which means the request may have been successful (no error). Let me try with the right body format and /api/send.\n\nWait, actually both commands ran in sequence. The first got error 1101, and the second got \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which is just the HTML response. So /api/send also returned 1101.\n\nWait, let me re-read: I see \"---\" and then \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". So the first curl got 1101, and the second curl got the HTML landing page. That means /api/send returned the homepage HTML, which suggests the POST to /api/send didn't work as expected.\n\n\nLet me reconsider the request body format for /send - maybe the properties need different names like \"thread\" instead of \"threadId\", or the endpoint expects a different JSON structure altogether. Since both endpoints are throwing 1101 exceptions, the worker itself seems to be failing when processing these requests.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-694a9440-1361-4e82-ae67-32be9dcfc195","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with minimal body\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{}' 2>&1\n\necho \"===\"\n\n# Try GET on send endpoint\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1090,"output":392,"cacheRead":17408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18890,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache